SQL Commands 
1. Update the Raspberry Pi system using the terminal 
commands: sudo apt update 
sudo apt upgrade -y 
2. Install MariaDB server on Raspberry 
Pi using: sudo apt install mariadb
server -y 
3. Start and enable the MariaDB service: 
sudo systemctl start 
mariadb sudo systemctl 
enable mariadb 
4. Open the MariaDB terminal using: 
sudo mysql 
5. Create a new MariaDB user and provide privileges: 
CREATE USER 'piuser'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED 
BY '1234'; GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON *.* TO 
'piuser'@'localhost'; FLUSH PRIVILEGES; 
6. Exit from 
MariaDB using: 
EXIT; 
7. Login again using the 
created user: mysql -u 
piuser -p 
8. Create a new database: 
CREATE DATABASE Raspberrypi; 
9. Select the 
database: 
USE 
Raspberrypi; 
10. Create a table named 
records: CREATE 
TABLE records ( 
id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY 
KEY, name VARCHAR(100), 
department 
VARCHAR(100), 
marks INT 
); 
11. Insert records into the table: 
INSERT INTO records (name, department, marks) 
VALUES 
('Arun', 'ECE', 85), 
('Kavin', 'CSE', 90), 
('Priya', 'EEE', 88); 
12. Display all 
records using: 
SELECT * FROM 
records; 
13. Update a 
record using: 
UPDATE records 
SET marks = 
95 WHERE 
id = 1; 
14. Delete 
record 
a 
using: 
DELETE FROM 
records WHERE 
id = 2; 
15. Display the final 
records table: SELECT * 
FROM records; 
16. Export the table into CSV 
format: SELECT * 
INTO OUTFILE 
'/tmp/records.csv' FIELDS 
TERMINATED BY ',' 
ENCLOSED BY '"' 
LINES TERMINATED BY '\n' 
FROM records; 
17. Exit from 
MariaDB using: 
EXIT; 
18. View the exported CSV 
file using: cat 
/tmp/records.csv
